WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.000
Fabric softener, household cleaners, and the never-mix rules.

2
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.300
This is the video for Module 4 of Liquid Soap, Shampoo and Disinfectants.

3
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:17.270
This module takes your range into the laundry room, the kitchen and the bathroom. First, a fabric softener.

4
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:22.980
Then a multipurpose spray, and a concentrate that saves offices money.

5
00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:32.180
Then a floor cleaner and a toilet descaler. Households, schools and churches buy these every week, so they bring repeat sales.

6
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:37.190
And most important, the mixing rules that keep your customers safe.

7
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:50.320
A softener uses a cationic surfactant called an esterquat. Cotton carries a slight negative charge in water, so the positive softener clings to the fibre and makes it feel soft.

8
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.070
Heat the water to the temperature on your supplier's data sheet.

9
00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:59.030
Warm the esterquat until soft or melted.

10
00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:04.590
Pour it slowly into the warm water while stirring. It turns milky white.

11
00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:15.780
Keep stirring as it cools, then add fragrance and preservative below about 40 degrees. If it is too thick, a little calcium chloride solution thins it.

12
00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:29.300
Softener and detergent combine into a sticky solid, so both stop working. Tell customers: wash and rinse with detergent first, then add softener to the final rinse water only.

13
00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:43.500
Her esterquat is about 90% active, and she uses 5.5% of it. That gives about 5% active, inside the normal 4 to 6% range for a standard softener.

14
00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:48.290
She sells a bottle at about 1,500 naira.

15
00:01:49.540 --> 00:02:01.010
1,000 ml divided by 30 ml is about 33 rinses. So the customer pays roughly 45 naira a wash, an easy number to compare with other brands.

16
00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:11.200
A multipurpose spray uses a low-foam nonionic surfactant and a little isopropyl alcohol, so it cleans and dries without streaks.

17
00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:21.650
Offices often prefer a concentrate. 1:19 means 1 part concentrate plus 19 parts water, 20 parts in total.

18
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:32.560
For example, Aisha in Abuja divides a 500 ml spray bottle by 20. Each refill needs 25 ml of concentrate.

19
00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.920
So one litre gives 40 refills.

20
00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:44.470
Her concentrate costs about 2,000 naira a litre, an approximate figure. That is about 50 naira a refill.

21
00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:53.780
She gives the office a 25 ml cup and a printed dilution card, and tests the diluted product herself before delivering.

22
00:02:55.030 --> 00:03:08.390
Toilet scale only dissolves in acid. A citric acid descaler is slower, but far safer to make, pack and use. It is thickened so it clings under the rim, and packed with a child-resistant cap.

23
00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:21.410
Many market products use hydrochloric acid. It gives off corrosive fumes, causes severe burns, and attacks fittings and grout. We do not recommend making it in a small workshop.

24
00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:34.780
Many customers believe two cleaners together will be stronger. Bleach and acids release chlorine gas, which damages the lungs. Bleach and ammonia release toxic chloramine gases.

25
00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:40.850
The safe rule: use one product, rinse or flush, then use the next, with the window open.

26
00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:50.090
If someone breathes in fumes from mixed cleaners, get them into fresh air at once and seek medical help. Do not go back into the closed bathroom.

27
00:03:51.340 --> 00:04:04.870
So remember. Softener goes in the final rinse. Work out dilutions and cost per use for your customers. Isopropyl alcohol is flammable, so mix away from flames, and test sprays on a hidden spot.

28
00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.820
And print the never-mix rules on every label.

29
00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:14.900
Now make a softener test batch, try your spray on three surfaces, and draft your warning label.

30
00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.190
Continue with the lessons below.
